WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.701 --> 00:00:03.367
♪♪

00:00:03.367 --> 00:00:04.868
-Hey, everybody. Welcome back.

00:00:04.868 --> 00:00:07.801
It's that time of week again.
Old Corrections.

00:00:07.801 --> 00:00:11.100
We're gonna just jump right
into it, if you don't mind.

00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:15.467
I think it was yesterday we were
talking about Rudy Giuliani

00:00:15.467 --> 00:00:18.300
using an Abraham Lincoln filter,

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:22.033
and we said he was talking
like a character

00:00:22.033 --> 00:00:25.100
from "Grand Theft Auto:
Civil War."

00:00:25.100 --> 00:00:27.100
A couple of you pointed out
it wouldn't be called that

00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:30.567
'cause there were no autos
during the Civil War.

00:00:30.567 --> 00:00:32.501
Would have to be
"Grand Theft Wagon"

00:00:32.501 --> 00:00:36.200
"Grand Theft Horse."

00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:38.400
It's just laziness
on Sal's part.

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:40.100
[ Laughter ]

00:00:42.834 --> 00:00:45.100
Last week in the monologue,

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:48.167
we had a joke about
the Philadelphia Flyers mascot,

00:00:48.167 --> 00:00:51.267
Gritty, being an anti-vaxxer,

00:00:51.267 --> 00:00:54.634
and a bunch of people
reached out to say,

00:00:54.634 --> 00:00:57.133
hey, Gritty has actually been

00:00:57.133 --> 00:01:01.467
a part of a pro-vaccine
campaign online.

00:01:01.467 --> 00:01:05.200
So we would like
to both apologize to Gritty

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:09.467
And point out to anyone
who is anti-vax

00:01:09.467 --> 00:01:12.200
that you are crazier
than [bleep] Gritty.

00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:13.801
[ Laughter ]

00:01:16.968 --> 00:01:19.834
This is very embarrassing.
I can't remember.

00:01:19.834 --> 00:01:22.200
It might have been
Monday's "Closer Look."

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:24.534
Miming a phone call...

00:01:24.534 --> 00:01:27.167
then went to get a pen...

00:01:27.167 --> 00:01:29.434
put the phone over here...

00:01:29.434 --> 00:01:31.534
and then leaned my head
that way.

00:01:31.534 --> 00:01:34.133
[ Laughter ]

00:01:34.133 --> 00:01:37.067
Which is a shame 'cause I --

00:01:37.067 --> 00:01:41.567
I don't want to toot
my own horn, but I feel like...

00:01:41.567 --> 00:01:45.734
when it comes to doing
one-sided phone-call comedy,

00:01:45.734 --> 00:01:48.901
I am the new Bob Newhart.

00:01:48.901 --> 00:01:51.267
The Bob Newhart, if you will.

00:01:51.267 --> 00:01:53.434
[ Laughter ]

00:01:57.534 --> 00:02:00.367
Graphics.

00:02:00.367 --> 00:02:03.667
Get to graphics, as I tend to.

00:02:03.667 --> 00:02:06.267
We talked about Donald Trump

00:02:06.267 --> 00:02:11.267
being gifted from Saudi Arabia
a cheetah fur robe,

00:02:11.267 --> 00:02:17.033
but in the graphic, he was
wearing a leopard-print robe.

00:02:17.033 --> 00:02:20.367
Now, I was pretty upset
about this, but then

00:02:20.367 --> 00:02:22.934
our head riser -- our head
writer, excuse me -- Alex Baze,

00:02:22.934 --> 00:02:26.334
came up to me and said,
"If you ask me...

00:02:26.334 --> 00:02:29.701
no matter what fur Donald Trump
wears, it's cheat-ah."

00:02:29.701 --> 00:02:31.667
And I was like, "Oof. Baze."

00:02:35.167 --> 00:02:36.934
Not your best, buddy.

00:02:36.934 --> 00:02:38.667
[ Laughter ]

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:45.767
We did a very well-received
10,000 Maniacs joke.

00:02:45.767 --> 00:02:48.200
[ Laughter ]

00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:50.567
But in the key,

00:02:50.567 --> 00:02:54.667
it was a photo of the band
in its current incarnation

00:02:54.667 --> 00:02:56.467
with lead singer Mary Ramsey

00:02:56.467 --> 00:02:59.501
and not Natalie Merchant.

00:02:59.501 --> 00:03:01.701
And...

00:03:01.701 --> 00:03:03.901
Pretty upset about it,
went down graphics,

00:03:03.901 --> 00:03:07.501
and said,
"Obviously, I'm very upset

00:03:07.501 --> 00:03:09.701
that you chose
to put in Mary Ramsey

00:03:09.701 --> 00:03:10.868
instead of Natalie Merchant.

00:03:10.868 --> 00:03:12.267
Do you have anything
to say about that?"

00:03:12.267 --> 00:03:14.400
And they said, "You're old."

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:16.133
[ Laughter ]

00:03:18.934 --> 00:03:21.300
This is the weird one
from Graphics this week

00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:24.634
that a lot of --
And just I think in general,

00:03:24.634 --> 00:03:26.634
if a band's lineup
changes graphics,

00:03:26.634 --> 00:03:28.701
you should check with me.

00:03:31.100 --> 00:03:34.701
You know what I mean?
If I talk about Genesis,

00:03:34.701 --> 00:03:36.000
don't just assume

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:39.434
I want Phil Collins
as the lead singer.

00:03:39.434 --> 00:03:42.534
I might want Peter Gabriel.

00:03:42.534 --> 00:03:45.567
I want the originals
more often than not.

00:03:49.133 --> 00:03:52.234
Especially with Genesis,
because that's

00:03:52.234 --> 00:03:55.367
what "Genesis" means.

00:03:55.367 --> 00:03:57.133
The origin!

00:03:58.767 --> 00:04:00.467
All right, so, we did --
We asked --

00:04:00.467 --> 00:04:04.400
Again, this is what
we ask Graphics.

00:04:04.400 --> 00:04:07.434
We're like,
"Hey, can we get a...

00:04:07.434 --> 00:04:11.300
angry grandpa at a Lowe's?"

00:04:11.300 --> 00:04:13.400
So a lot of people are like,
"Hey, why is it

00:04:13.400 --> 00:04:16.033
aisle 61, aisle 62...

00:04:16.033 --> 00:04:18.901
and then aisle 17?"

00:04:18.901 --> 00:04:20.300
And I got to be honest.

00:04:20.300 --> 00:04:23.234
I'm like 50/50
this is some QAnon [bleep].

00:04:23.234 --> 00:04:25.734
[ Laughter ]

00:04:25.734 --> 00:04:28.734
Like, it would surprise me
not at all

00:04:28.734 --> 00:04:32.200
if the Graphics Department
were full Q believers

00:04:32.200 --> 00:04:36.300
who are sending signals
and messages out...

00:04:36.300 --> 00:04:37.968
to their ilk.

00:04:42.767 --> 00:04:44.734
I went down and I said,
"What do you think happened

00:04:44.734 --> 00:04:46.000
on January 6th?"

00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:48.100
And they said, "A gathering."

00:04:48.100 --> 00:04:49.968
[ Laughter ]

00:04:54.567 --> 00:04:56.133
Monologue joke.

00:04:56.133 --> 00:04:59.567
We told a monologue joke
about how some lions

00:04:59.567 --> 00:05:04.601
at a zoo
tested positive for COVID

00:05:04.601 --> 00:05:08.367
and that the lions
are doing fine

00:05:08.367 --> 00:05:10.367
and they're certainly
doing better

00:05:10.367 --> 00:05:13.634
than whoever it was
that had to give them a swab.

00:05:13.634 --> 00:05:17.701
And then we showed a tombstone
that said "R.I.P."

00:05:17.701 --> 00:05:19.501
And someone wrote,

00:05:19.501 --> 00:05:21.667
"Tombstones
don't just say 'R.I.P.'

00:05:21.667 --> 00:05:23.234
They have a person's name

00:05:23.234 --> 00:05:27.267
and, you know, the dates
of their birth and death."

00:05:27.267 --> 00:05:29.601
And then this is what
I've come to really enjoy,

00:05:29.601 --> 00:05:32.467
which is sort of
cross-jackal talk.

00:05:32.467 --> 00:05:33.801
Someone else jumped in and said,

00:05:33.801 --> 00:05:36.834
"Maybe in this case,
'R.I.P.' was cause of death."

00:05:38.634 --> 00:05:40.434
[ Laughter ]

00:05:42.067 --> 00:05:43.968
"I have bad news, ma'am.
Your husband wandered

00:05:43.968 --> 00:05:46.701
into the lion cage,
and there was a rip."

00:05:46.701 --> 00:05:48.601
[ Laughter ]

00:05:51.801 --> 00:05:54.367
Congratulations are in order.
I hope you guys don't mind

00:05:54.367 --> 00:05:57.167
that I'm gonna take a little
time out from Corrections.

00:05:57.167 --> 00:06:01.300
I would like to congratulate
my dear friend Colin Jost,

00:06:01.300 --> 00:06:03.801
who on Saturday passed me

00:06:03.801 --> 00:06:07.567
as the longest-serving
"Weekend Update" anchor.

00:06:07.567 --> 00:06:10.801
155 episodes
hosted by Colin Jost.

00:06:10.801 --> 00:06:13.601
And I'm so proud of him.

00:06:13.601 --> 00:06:15.367
I think he and Che
do a great job.

00:06:15.367 --> 00:06:17.234
A few people
have come up to me and said,

00:06:17.234 --> 00:06:19.667
"Did it make you sad
to have your record broken?"

00:06:19.667 --> 00:06:22.501
And, um, I moved on.

00:06:22.501 --> 00:06:23.968
Okay?

00:06:23.968 --> 00:06:25.634
[ Laughter ]

00:06:25.634 --> 00:06:28.467
I'm good.

00:06:28.467 --> 00:06:30.367
On my own terms!

00:06:33.801 --> 00:06:35.834
And I've got a job!

00:06:38.100 --> 00:06:40.234
I mean, I've hosted
like 1,200 of these,

00:06:40.234 --> 00:06:42.501
while Jost has done his 155.

00:06:42.501 --> 00:06:44.667
I got an everyday job.

00:06:44.667 --> 00:06:49.434
Old fat-cat Jost
doing once a week?

00:06:49.434 --> 00:06:51.200
Rolling out on Saturday,

00:06:51.200 --> 00:06:52.934
You're all throwing crowns
at his feet?

00:06:52.934 --> 00:06:55.100
No, thank you!

00:06:55.100 --> 00:06:58.901
Also, he has had it easy.

00:06:58.901 --> 00:07:04.100
All his "Updates," most of them
during the Trump era...

00:07:04.100 --> 00:07:06.200
when the jokes wrote themselves.

00:07:06.200 --> 00:07:09.467
And they did -- for us, too.

00:07:09.467 --> 00:07:12.701
A lot of people said, "Did
the jokes write themselves?"

00:07:12.701 --> 00:07:14.234
And they did.

00:07:14.234 --> 00:07:16.234
We would leave, and we'd
just come back to the office,

00:07:16.234 --> 00:07:17.968
and the jokes would be there.

00:07:17.968 --> 00:07:19.667
[ Laughter ]

00:07:19.667 --> 00:07:21.234
Do you know the story?

00:07:21.234 --> 00:07:23.167
Shoemaker?
The shoemaker and the elves?

00:07:23.167 --> 00:07:24.934
It was like that.

00:07:24.934 --> 00:07:27.667
Except we didn't have, like,
a kindly old shoemaker.

00:07:27.667 --> 00:07:30.968
We had our Shoemaker.

00:07:30.968 --> 00:07:32.167
So every night he'd be like,

00:07:32.167 --> 00:07:33.734
"You elves better
write these jokes,

00:07:33.734 --> 00:07:36.300
or I'm throwing you
out the window!"

00:07:36.300 --> 00:07:39.601
[ Laughter ]

00:07:39.601 --> 00:07:42.501
"I'm gonna stick one of those
pointy-toed boots

00:07:42.501 --> 00:07:44.100
up your you-know-what!"

00:07:44.100 --> 00:07:45.467
[ Laughter ]

00:07:45.467 --> 00:07:47.467
And I'd say, "Shoemaker,
don't yell at the elves."

00:07:47.467 --> 00:07:51.434
And he goes, "Oh, yeah?
Now we can't yell at the elves?!

00:07:51.434 --> 00:07:54.367
This is cancel culture
run amok!"

00:07:54.367 --> 00:07:56.901
[ Laughter ]

00:07:56.901 --> 00:07:58.367
I go,
"What does that even mean?"

00:07:58.367 --> 00:07:59.968
He goes,
"I don't know what it means.

00:07:59.968 --> 00:08:01.667
I just know if you say it,
cha-ching."

00:08:01.667 --> 00:08:03.400
I was like, "What?"

00:08:03.400 --> 00:08:05.367
[ Laughter ]

00:08:05.367 --> 00:08:06.801
I'm like...

00:08:06.801 --> 00:08:10.834
I feel like this is bills.
Like dollar bills. Cha-ching.

00:08:10.834 --> 00:08:13.033
[ Laughter ]

00:08:16.601 --> 00:08:19.300
Scollins wrote this joke.

00:08:19.300 --> 00:08:21.400
Amid global supply chain delays,

00:08:21.400 --> 00:08:23.534
toy makers are reportedly
planning to release

00:08:23.534 --> 00:08:25.901
more small, squishy toys
this holiday season.

00:08:25.901 --> 00:08:28.968
"You mean rabbits?"
asked Lennie.

00:08:28.968 --> 00:08:32.000
And then we showed Lennie
from "Of Mice and Men."

00:08:32.000 --> 00:08:36.000
I then -- I referred to it
as "Mice and Men,"

00:08:36.000 --> 00:08:39.067
and a bunch of people jumped out
and said it's "Of Mice and Men."

00:08:39.067 --> 00:08:42.400
So apologies to...
John Steinbeck.

00:08:43.734 --> 00:08:48.167
And then a teacher...
reached out to say,

00:08:48.167 --> 00:08:52.467
"You know, I'm actually teaching
this right now to my sophomores,

00:08:52.467 --> 00:08:56.501
and the joke doesn't work
because..."

00:08:56.501 --> 00:08:58.000
And I should note --

00:08:58.000 --> 00:09:00.434
there's nothing novel
about finding

00:09:00.434 --> 00:09:03.300
why a Scollins joke
doesn't work.

00:09:03.300 --> 00:09:07.367
[ Laughter ]

00:09:07.367 --> 00:09:11.367
But she said
Lennie dreamed of rabbits,

00:09:11.367 --> 00:09:12.734
but in the book,

00:09:12.734 --> 00:09:16.934
Lennie only killed a puppy
and Curley's wife.

00:09:16.934 --> 00:09:18.934
To which I wanted to say...

00:09:18.934 --> 00:09:21.934
"She has a name!"

00:09:21.934 --> 00:09:25.100
But then I looked it up.
She doesn't.

00:09:25.100 --> 00:09:28.200
Whole book.
Just "Curley's wife."

00:09:28.200 --> 00:09:30.234
How about that?

00:09:30.234 --> 00:09:32.501
And then Steinbeck reached out.

00:09:32.501 --> 00:09:35.901
[ Laughter ]

00:09:35.901 --> 00:09:37.534
he didn't reach out,
but I read a quote.

00:09:37.534 --> 00:09:39.334
I found an old Steinbeck quote.

00:09:39.334 --> 00:09:42.200
And he actually said
there was a reason Curley's wife

00:09:42.200 --> 00:09:44.000
was only ever referred to
as Curley's wife,

00:09:44.000 --> 00:09:46.200
which is she was not a person.
She was a symbol.

00:09:46.200 --> 00:09:49.701
She was there to serve
as a foil for Lennie,

00:09:49.701 --> 00:09:53.100
a danger to Lennie.

00:09:53.100 --> 00:09:54.601
But I think
that's just an excuse.

00:09:54.601 --> 00:09:56.200
I think Steinbeck
was just, like, bad

00:09:56.200 --> 00:09:59.968
at coming up with names.

00:09:59.968 --> 00:10:01.667
You know what I mean?

00:10:01.667 --> 00:10:03.033
The original "Mice and Men"

00:10:03.033 --> 00:10:05.234
was just called
"Smarty Pants and Big Guy."

00:10:05.234 --> 00:10:08.601
[ Laughter ]

00:10:08.601 --> 00:10:12.400
Or he had a perfect name...

00:10:12.400 --> 00:10:13.801
and he couldn't remember it.

00:10:13.801 --> 00:10:16.200
You know, sometimes you write...

00:10:16.200 --> 00:10:17.767
and you have something --
you know you have something.

00:10:17.767 --> 00:10:19.501
You think about it before you're
falling to bed or whatever,

00:10:19.501 --> 00:10:21.133
and you wake up,
you can't remember it.

00:10:21.133 --> 00:10:22.968
And then you can't come up
with anything else

00:10:22.968 --> 00:10:24.667
'cause you know
you have the perfect one.

00:10:24.667 --> 00:10:27.968
And I'm sure his editor
came over and was like,

00:10:27.968 --> 00:10:30.334
"You don't remember the name,
do you?

00:10:30.334 --> 00:10:32.267
That's why it's 'Curley's wife.'
You don't remember the name."

00:10:32.267 --> 00:10:34.334
And he said,
"Of course I remember it."

00:10:34.334 --> 00:10:37.000
And the editor said,
"What is it?"

00:10:37.000 --> 00:10:39.267
And Steinbeck said...

00:10:39.267 --> 00:10:41.100
"Mulva?"

00:10:41.100 --> 00:10:42.834
[ Laughter ]

00:10:49.200 --> 00:10:52.100
"Laurie-ohla?"

00:10:52.100 --> 00:10:55.033
And then the editor left.

00:10:55.033 --> 00:10:57.968
And then Steinbeck was like...

00:10:57.968 --> 00:11:02.701
And he ran to the window, and
he yelled down to the editor,

00:11:02.701 --> 00:11:04.167
and he said, "Dolores!"

00:11:04.167 --> 00:11:07.501
[ "Seinfeld" riff plays ]

00:11:07.501 --> 00:11:09.434
[ Laughter ]

00:11:20.701 --> 00:11:23.601
We told a Baby Hitler joke
this week.

00:11:23.601 --> 00:11:26.501
Because we like to laugh.
[ Chuckles ]

00:11:26.501 --> 00:11:28.200
Do we have
the Baby Hitler photo?

00:11:28.200 --> 00:11:29.868
There we go. Um...

00:11:29.868 --> 00:11:34.467
I mean, it took so long
to find a kid with the mustache.

00:11:34.467 --> 00:11:37.400
You can put it down.
[ Chuckles ]

00:11:37.400 --> 00:11:41.067
So, this was interesting.
Someone, um...

00:11:41.067 --> 00:11:42.534
[ Chuckles ]

00:11:42.534 --> 00:11:44.734
Someone wrote a Correction,

00:11:44.734 --> 00:11:46.501
and then I noticed
that the first line of the --

00:11:46.501 --> 00:11:48.267
It said "Correction,"
but then there was a line

00:11:48.267 --> 00:11:50.934
through the "Correction,"
which they had gone back --

00:11:50.934 --> 00:11:54.868
They had edited their own
comment, because they said,

00:11:54.868 --> 00:11:58.133
hey, Hitler doesn't have
blue eyes. He had brown eyes.

00:11:58.133 --> 00:11:59.934
Brown hair, brown eyes.

00:11:59.934 --> 00:12:01.968
Obviously used a stock photo
of a baby with blue eyes,

00:12:01.968 --> 00:12:04.200
but that couldn't
have been Baby Hitler.

00:12:04.200 --> 00:12:06.434
And then someone else --

00:12:06.434 --> 00:12:11.367
Again, cross-jackal discourse --

00:12:11.367 --> 00:12:12.934
said, "Correction of Correction.

00:12:12.934 --> 00:12:14.567
He actually had blue eyes
and brown hair,

00:12:14.567 --> 00:12:16.567
and since most pictures of him
are black-and-white,

00:12:16.567 --> 00:12:18.300
people tend to assume
that he had brown eyes

00:12:18.300 --> 00:12:19.767
to go along with his hair
and his uniform.

00:12:19.767 --> 00:12:22.734
There are many statements
by eyewitnesses confirming

00:12:22.734 --> 00:12:24.200
that he had blue eyes,

00:12:24.200 --> 00:12:27.501
including by Goebbels."
[gerbuhlz]

00:12:27.501 --> 00:12:30.934
And if you can't trust
Goebbels...

00:12:30.934 --> 00:12:33.434
I feel like I'm saying
his name wrong, but...

00:12:33.434 --> 00:12:36.234
This is great. I think
I've talked about this before.

00:12:36.234 --> 00:12:38.234
When I'm not sure
I'm pronouncing something right,

00:12:38.234 --> 00:12:39.868
I waste my time
and I go on YouTube

00:12:39.868 --> 00:12:42.100
to one of those
"how to pronounce things."

00:12:42.100 --> 00:12:44.534
And you type in
"how to pronounce Goebbels."

00:12:44.534 --> 00:12:45.767
And then it's that thing

00:12:45.767 --> 00:12:49.601
where a swirl comes in
and then says the name.

00:12:49.601 --> 00:12:52.601
And the only reason
I'm bringing it up...

00:12:52.601 --> 00:12:54.300
is, again, you enter in

00:12:54.300 --> 00:12:55.868
"how to pronounce
Joseph Goebbels,"

00:12:55.868 --> 00:12:57.934
then you hit "play,"
and there was a pre-roll ad

00:12:57.934 --> 00:13:00.434
for, like, a clothing company.

00:13:00.434 --> 00:13:01.868
[ Laughs ]
And so it was, like,

00:13:01.868 --> 00:13:03.501
super-young, beautiful people
being like...

00:13:03.501 --> 00:13:05.000
♪ Da-na, deh-deh-deh-deh-deh ♪

00:13:05.000 --> 00:13:07.434
And then it was like,
"Joseph Goebbels!"

00:13:07.434 --> 00:13:09.334
[ Laughter ]

00:13:11.601 --> 00:13:15.868
I've talked about
how some people have said, um...

00:13:15.868 --> 00:13:17.601
"I don't believe
you have an audience.

00:13:17.601 --> 00:13:18.968
I think it's a laugh track."

00:13:18.968 --> 00:13:21.467
And we addressed this last week,
that it's an audience.

00:13:21.467 --> 00:13:24.234
In the beginning of the show,
there's a reverse shot.

00:13:24.234 --> 00:13:25.667
That's the only time
we show them.

00:13:25.667 --> 00:13:27.334
But that should prove
there's an audience.

00:13:27.334 --> 00:13:28.734
There is a --

00:13:28.734 --> 00:13:31.601
There was a comment
that I have to read

00:13:31.601 --> 00:13:33.334
because I will admit --

00:13:33.334 --> 00:13:37.367
Very, very mean,
but I enjoyed it a great deal.

00:13:37.367 --> 00:13:38.801
They think it's a laugh track

00:13:38.801 --> 00:13:42.100
because they can't believe
you get actual humans to laugh.

00:13:42.100 --> 00:13:44.300
[ Laughter ]

00:13:48.434 --> 00:13:50.667
My second-favorite comment
of the week.

00:13:50.667 --> 00:13:53.334
[ Chuckles ]

00:13:53.334 --> 00:13:57.534
Scollins. I know he keeps
coming up. I apologize.

00:13:57.534 --> 00:14:02.534
Scollins wrote a joke --
he's from Massachusetts --

00:14:02.534 --> 00:14:04.667
ragging on his home state
a little bit.

00:14:04.667 --> 00:14:07.067
I don't know if this is why
this person wrote this,

00:14:07.067 --> 00:14:10.067
but the hyper-specificity of it
is so New England

00:14:10.067 --> 00:14:12.000
that I enjoyed a great deal.

00:14:12.000 --> 00:14:13.868
I'm gonna read it
with a Boston accent.

00:14:13.868 --> 00:14:17.133
I don't know if this person
actually has one or not,

00:14:17.133 --> 00:14:18.801
so this is poetic license.

00:14:18.801 --> 00:14:20.868
[Boston accent]
"Ask Scollins why his town

00:14:20.868 --> 00:14:22.834
doesn't have a decent hotel!"

00:14:22.834 --> 00:14:24.834
[ Laughter ]

00:14:31.601 --> 00:14:34.100
Um, my former nemesis --

00:14:34.100 --> 00:14:36.534
I wore this last time out
when we did this --

00:14:36.534 --> 00:14:39.367
Patty Lyons...

00:14:39.367 --> 00:14:42.567
seamstress extraordinaire...

00:14:42.567 --> 00:14:45.501
made this Jackal Power hat,
and then at the end, I said --

00:14:45.501 --> 00:14:47.501
I revealed
that it was double-sided,

00:14:47.501 --> 00:14:49.334
and I showed the other side
of it, and then a lot of people

00:14:49.334 --> 00:14:52.934
said all hats are double-sided.

00:14:52.934 --> 00:14:55.968
If it has -- If it has one side,
it's a picture of a hat.

00:15:02.701 --> 00:15:06.167
I give Graphics a hard time.
I really do.

00:15:06.167 --> 00:15:07.968
But...

00:15:07.968 --> 00:15:09.701
Tara in Graphics.

00:15:09.701 --> 00:15:11.767
Every week,
pretty much every week,

00:15:11.767 --> 00:15:15.767
I request --
not with a lot of warning --

00:15:15.767 --> 00:15:17.467
a different mug.

00:15:17.467 --> 00:15:20.200
And for Halloween,
I had a couple of ideas.

00:15:20.200 --> 00:15:21.634
And I'm not gonna tell you.

00:15:21.634 --> 00:15:23.400
I think you guys can
figure out over there.

00:15:23.400 --> 00:15:25.734
So, there's --
there's one, right?

00:15:25.734 --> 00:15:29.133
Think we all know.

00:15:29.133 --> 00:15:31.400
But this one, I'm really --
This one's, like, a deeper cut.

00:15:31.400 --> 00:15:35.834
This one's, like, for obvious,
like, basic jackals.

00:15:35.834 --> 00:15:37.734
This one...

00:15:39.067 --> 00:15:41.501
There's that one there.

00:15:41.501 --> 00:15:43.968
And I think we're gonna...

00:15:43.968 --> 00:15:47.701
We're gonna post these
at @seacaptainpolls

00:15:47.701 --> 00:15:49.834
to get your vote
for the favorite.

00:15:49.834 --> 00:15:53.133
And also these are available

00:15:53.133 --> 00:15:56.567
online at w-w-w-w...

00:15:56.567 --> 00:15:59.868
[ Laughter ]

00:15:59.868 --> 00:16:01.701
...dot late night merch...

00:16:01.701 --> 00:16:03.934
front slash jackal.

00:16:03.934 --> 00:16:06.267
[ Laughter ]

00:16:06.267 --> 00:16:11.701
♪ These are the days ♪

00:16:11.701 --> 00:16:13.634
♪ To remember ♪

00:16:16.067 --> 00:16:20.033
♪ Never before and never since ♪

00:16:20.033 --> 00:16:22.067
♪ I promise ♪

00:16:23.901 --> 00:16:26.901
For "Weekend Update,"
I'm Seth Meyers.

00:16:26.901 --> 00:16:28.968
Good night.

